{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the fix in [scheduler.py](/workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py) and wrote the report to [root_cause.md](/workspace/out/root_cause.md).\n\nThe root cause was production nondeterminism in the scheduler itself: it accepted injected `clock` and `random_source` dependencies but still used global `time.time()` and `random.random()`, and `ready()` randomized equal-priority tasks with `shuffle()` before sorting only by priority. I changed it to use the injected clock/random source everywhere and to sort ready tasks deterministically with `(-priority, run_at, created_at, id)`.\n\nVerification in this container:\n- `python3 -m compileall flakyqueue`\n- A direct `python3` assertion script covering the same behaviors as `tests/test_scheduler.py` and `tests/test_retry_order.py`\n\nI could not run the exact requested `python -m pytest tests` here because this environment does not have `python`, `pytest`, `pip`, or `ensurepip`; only `/usr/bin/python3` is present. The report documents that limitation explicitly."}}
